From 2fa58c6140eff058bf6c71ee37ba601a84242e41 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Stefane Fermigier <sf@abilian.com>
Date: Tue, 22 Sep 2026 09:55:52 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 21/82] OdfFile: stop overruling the note style's indent and
 line spacing

Writing ODT, the converter stamps a 0.2cm hanging indent and a 100% line
height onto the automatic style of every footnote and endnote body
paragraph. An automatic style overrides the style:parent-style-name
chain, so this silently replaces whatever the author's note style asks
for, including the style the same conversion has just written correctly
into styles.xml.

Measured: a note style declaring fo:margin-left 2cm, fo:text-indent -2cm
and fo:line-height 200% comes back as 0.2cm, -0.2cm and 100%. The
intermediate DOCX is faithful on this point, carrying w:ind and w:spacing
in the style with only a w:pStyle on the paragraph, and LibreOffice fed
the identical file writes no automatic style at all and keeps the
author's values.

Two changes.

The line height had no business here. Nothing about a hanging indent
concerns line spacing, there was no test for it, and it fired as
collateral whenever the indent default fired. Removed.

The indent default now applies only when the paragraph names no style,
so nothing in the style chain could supply one. The guard previously
inspected the paragraph's direct w:pPr alone, which cannot see indent
that arrives through w:pStyle, so it fired in the ordinary case where the
paragraph carries nothing but a style reference.

Note the consequence, which is a judgement call worth confirming: Word
writes its footnote paragraphs with <w:pStyle w:val="FootnoteText"/> and
no direct indent, so those now render flush rather than hanging. That is
what LibreOffice produces from the same input, and Word itself does not
show a hanging indent there, but it is a visible change for
Word-sourced documents.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 OdfFile/Writer/Converter/DocxConverter.cpp | 11 +++++++++--
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/OdfFile/Writer/Converter/DocxConverter.cpp b/OdfFile/Writer/Converter/DocxConverter.cpp
index 6afb61f79f..24653fc40d 100644
--- a/OdfFile/Writer/Converter/DocxConverter.cpp
+++ b/OdfFile/Writer/Converter/DocxConverter.cpp
@@ -1769,12 +1769,19 @@ void DocxConverter::convert(OOX::Logic::CParagraphProperty	*oox_paragraph_pr,
 
 	}
 
+	// A default hanging indent for note bodies, for documents that state none.
+	// It lands on an automatic style, which wins over the style chain, so it may
+	// only be applied when nothing in that chain could supply one: a paragraph
+	// that names a style inherits from it, and this must not overrule it.
+	// fo_line_height_ used to be set here too. It was collateral, nothing about
+	// a hanging indent concerns line spacing, and it silently replaced whatever
+	// spacing the note style asked for.
 	if (odt_context->notes_context()->is_started()	&& !paragraph_properties->fo_margin_left_ 
-													&& !paragraph_properties->fo_text_indent_)
+													&& !paragraph_properties->fo_text_indent_
+													&& !oox_paragraph_pr->m_oPStyle.IsInit())
 	{
 		paragraph_properties->fo_margin_left_			= odf_types::length( 0.2, odf_types::length::cm);	
 		paragraph_properties->fo_text_indent_			= odf_types::length(-0.2, odf_types::length::cm);
-		paragraph_properties->fo_line_height_			= odf_types::percent(100.); 
 		paragraph_properties->style_auto_text_indent_	= false;
 	}
 
